# tree_mg5_tpole.mg5 -- the MadGraph runs of tree_mg5.mg5 again with the grid of mg5_tpole.py for massive t-channel invariants
# (research note models/spinor_qed, steps (2) and (6)).  Run from Src/ after tree_mg5.mg5 and mg5_tpole.py:
#   mg5_aMC tree_mg5_tpole.mg5 > work/tree_mg5_tpole.log   (run_tree_check.sh does this)
# Processes (A)-(D) at sqrt(s) = 4, 6, 10 with the settings of the main runs of tree_mg5.mg5 (10000 events, cuts off,
# (B) at |cos theta| < 0.9), in this order, then (C) at sqrt(s) = 4 with 100000 events (tree_sigma.py relies on the order).
# The copied run_cards hold the last run of each directory, so every setting that differs is set again.  Only (C) (u-channel
# electron) and (D) (t- and u-channel electron) have massive t-channel propagators; (A) (s channel) and (B) (massless photon in
# the t channel) keep MadGraph's own grid and test that the patch changes nothing else.
set automatic_html_opening False
launch work/mg5_treeA_tpole
0
set nevents 10000
set ebeam1 2.0
set ebeam2 2.0
0
launch work/mg5_treeA_tpole
0
set ebeam1 3.0
set ebeam2 3.0
0
launch work/mg5_treeA_tpole
0
set ebeam1 5.0
set ebeam2 5.0
0
launch work/mg5_treeB_tpole
0
set nevents 10000
set ebeam1 2.0
set ebeam2 2.0
set etal 1.04389844857
0
launch work/mg5_treeB_tpole
0
set ebeam1 3.0
set ebeam2 3.0
set etal 1.25087255895
0
launch work/mg5_treeB_tpole
0
set ebeam1 5.0
set ebeam2 5.0
set etal 1.38387628971
0
launch work/mg5_treeC_tpole
0
set nevents 10000
set etal -1
set ebeam1 2.125000000000
set ebeam2 1.875000000000
0
launch work/mg5_treeC_tpole
0
set ebeam1 3.083333333333
set ebeam2 2.916666666667
0
launch work/mg5_treeC_tpole
0
set ebeam1 5.050000000000
set ebeam2 4.950000000000
0
launch work/mg5_treeD_tpole
0
set nevents 10000
set ebeam1 2.0
set ebeam2 2.0
0
launch work/mg5_treeD_tpole
0
set ebeam1 3.0
set ebeam2 3.0
0
launch work/mg5_treeD_tpole
0
set ebeam1 5.0
set ebeam2 5.0
0
launch work/mg5_treeC_tpole
0
set nevents 100000
set ebeam1 2.125000000000
set ebeam2 1.875000000000
0
